{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:1b033c8d3aeb463ea09fd6858bae04b27a79da1a6d381b6cabee35b011058082","title":"Can a spacetime big bang be described by gauge degrees of freedom that become tractable when the string geometry fails? The reviewed null linear-dilaton construction exchanges early strong string coupling for weak worldvolume Yang–Mills coupling.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b78587762045c393aa696677de10213a9369530ad072a1f940e9f7e0476d21c","title":"Can a minimal hidden non-Abelian gauge sector on a five-dimensional orbifold generate a sufficiently flat inflaton potential without additional charged matter, support observationally acceptable inflation, and reheat through gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b3f60d668b6e5e34f7d802825aca8a7da3d450a02c8871cc663009dcd0c4c9b","title":"How can dynamical, possibly metastable supersymmetry breaking at low energies produce viable gauge-mediated soft terms, address flavor and hierarchy problems, and motivate possible collider phenomenology?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b37134cfa7a20619ae8745dd91daf5904952a3ef9c31712b33206d96a6cc922","title":"Can two Kähler inflatons produce successive inflationary stages whose weak interaction preserves information about the first stage as a sharp curvature-spectrum peak, and can such a peak improve the historical WMAP7 temperature-spectrum fit near ℓ ≃ 40?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0009"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1bf8d448385ec0395bf51790b285147f22edddcd759f2037e5cd9a6259bfae3c","title":"Can gauge-field backreaction at order α′ be computed in he