 leading potentials arise when two complex-structure saxions grow with a fixed ordering? An ordered degeneration determines weights, and each weight supplies a permitted Laurent monomial in the two saxions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b8f0e2f4775166f3d147b751b06640675f79830cbb41407c956f91748e3751c","title":"How can supersymmetry, string compactification and a possible multiverse address the electroweak and cosmological-constant naturalness problems, and what prevents accommodation of small parameters from becoming a predictive explanation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1bb0ee4ef89f395e9d60f164d6e34a60417ca750f31d66ff7bd626f3ee936f23","title":"How do flux geometry and gravitational descendants determine holomorphic, modular and elliptic anomalies of genus-zero partition functions on elliptic Calabi–Yau fourfolds, and explain derivative relations between flux sectors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b6fb30e1df872f7b97ac8ae392b8b9c0132bc9b200c2fae7abb7198d65fe204","title":"Must interactions producing heavy states through graviton scattering be suppressed by Newton's constant? Maximal supersymmetry provides a special setting where four-point graviton polarizations can be factored out and dispersive measurements become simpler.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1b956de67dae8df414add800d9ab7fb8ff6bdd65c614d7779be975640f434961","title":"How small can flux-induced tadpole charge be while stabilizing every flux-stabilizable modulus away from singularities, and can differential evolution plus local search find the relevant minima for K3×K3 and related indefinite lattices?","con